    "raw": "We will loosen the subtask / parent / task / INFO relation model. Fold all the relation commands into one: todo relate --id <id> <ID-RELATIONSHIPNAME> <other> <OTHER-RELATIONSHIPNAME>... -- i.e. one command names the relationship from each side, replacing the current scattered mechanisms (set --parent make-it-so writes, add-subtodo's Subtodos registration, INFO back-links, merge bookkeeping's State flips). Groom notes: (1) enumerate today's relationship kinds and their storage shape -- Parent[] refs on the child, Subtodos[] rows on the parent with State tracked/INFO/merged; (2) decide the relationship vocabulary (e.g. PARENT/CHILD, TRACKS/TRACKED-BY, INFO) and whether both sides are always named explicitly as in the example; (3) relate must stay store-only (no branch checkout, no commit), consistent with the id-only selector model; (4) existing commands become sugar over relate or are removed. User expects this to be fairly straightforward."
  },
